### Page 5 of 17

```text
UDC-22-00425-02
January 3, 2023
RECOMMENDED MOTION:

Move to approve the Dell Range Addition, 6th Filing Expedited Preliminary Plat, advancing the Final Plat
to the Governing Body, with a recommended exception to block size.

APPLICABLE CITY CODE SECTION(S) AND PLANS:

UDC 2.1.2 Preliminary Plat Approval

UDC 2.1.3 Final Plat Approval

UDC Article 4 Subdivisions

UDC Article 5 Zoning Regulations

PlanCheyenne

BACKGROUND:

The applicant is requesting approval of a plat to combine parcels into one large lot for multifamily
development. The resulting lot would be approximately 10.7 acres.

SURROUNDING LAND USE AND ZONING:

ANALYSIS OF APPLICATION CONFORMANCE WITH REVIEW CRITERIA:

Should the Planning Commission wish to recommend approval of the Preliminary Plat, the Commission
must make the following findings required in UDC 2.1.2.d   a detailed analysis is below:

1) The application is in accordance with the development policies and physical patterns
identified in the Comprehensive Plan. (UDC 2.1.2.d.1)

The future land use map within PlanCheyenne identifies this area as developing with a mix of
residential uses, and the proposed plat in the proposed zoning district would be compatible with
this objective. PlanCheyenne supports the use of existing infrastructure and timely provision of
services (including emergency and education services). This development is proposed in an area
which has largely existing infrastructure and no expansion of infrastructure is necessary. The
property is within the Urban Service Boundary and has access to all utilities.

The application complies with this review criterion.

